              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "nāvāle, nāvālis — \"a dockyard, a place where ships are kept\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "In nāvālī fabrī nāvēs novās aedificant. In the dockyard the workmen build new ships."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Third declension, neuter: nāvāle, nāvālis n., often plural nāvālia. It is the neuter of the adjective nāvālis 'of ships'; English naval comes from that."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "nāvāle is the neuter of the adjective nāvālis 'of ships', built on nāvis 'ship' (Lewis & Short). English naval comes from the adjective."
            }
          ]
