              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "aestuārium, aestuāriī — \"a tidal inlet, a tidal marsh; an estuary\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Ubi mare recēdit, in aestuāriō lutum est. When the sea goes back, there is mud in the tidal inlet."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Second declension, neuter: aestuārium, aestuāriī n. Land the tide covers and uncovers. English estuary comes from it."
            }
          ]
        },
