          "title": "You'll want to know: pharus, pharī",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "pharus, pharī — \"a lighthouse\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Nocte lūx pharī procul ardet, et nautae portum inveniunt. At night the light of the lighthouse burns far off, and the sailors find the harbour."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Second declension, feminine: pharus, pharī f. (also pharos). Named after a famous lighthouse island."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "pharus was borrowed from Greek pharos, the name of the island whose lighthouse became famous (EtymDB; Lewis & Short); the name then became the common word for any lighthouse."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
